    "result_text": "The implementation is complete and the full test suite passes (`BUILD SUCCESS`, 1 test, 0 failures).\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the `riskFlag` field on owners per the spec: **true when the owner is a possible duplicate, the email domain is disposable-adjacent, or the city is over its soft capacity; false otherwise.**\n\nThe change reuses existing signals rather than recomputing them, and keeps each piece of logic in its natural home:\n\n1. **`model/DisposableEmailDomains.java`** (new) \u2014 a small static utility that owns the disposable-domain blocklist as a single source of truth. It exposes `isDisposable` (exact match, for the hard-reject at create/update) and `isDisposableAdjacent` (a known disposable domain, a subdomain of one, or a domain sharing its registrable base label under a different TLD \u2014 the near-misses that slip past the exact blocklist).\n\n2. **`rest/validation/EmailNormalizer.java`** \u2014 refactored `isDisposable` to delegate to the new utility, removing the duplicated blocklist and inline domain-parsing. This also lets the entity reuse the same knowledge without depending on a Spring `@Component`.\n\n3. **`model/Owner.java`** \u2014 added a derived, transient `getRiskFlag()` that ORs the three signals: the already-stamped `possibleDuplicate`, the already-stamped `capacityWarning` (the city being at/over its soft capacity of 40, one short of the hard limit of 50), and `DisposableEmailDomains.isDisposableAdjacent(email)`. It follows the same pattern as the other derived getters (`getOwnerSegment`, `getAgeBand`, etc.).\n\n4. **`resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 added the read-only `riskFlag` boolean to the `OwnerFields` schema so the generated `OwnerDto` carries it and MapStruct auto-maps it from `Owner.getRiskFlag()` (no explicit `@Mapping` needed, consistent with the other derived fields).\n\nThe acceptance test `coreRiskFlagFalseNormally` \u2014 which creates a normal owner (no duplicate, no email, unfilled city) and expects `riskFlag: false` \u2014 passes.",
